<title>USA: 17-state hog and pig inventory--USDA.</title>
<headline>17-state hog and pig inventory--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA hog and pig inventory in the 17 major producing states, with the current period as a percent of prior year's period.</p>
<p> (1,000 head):  Pct   3/1/97   3/1/96</p>
<p> All Hogs/Pigs  100   51,730   51,940</p>
<p> For Breeding   101    6,240    6,165</p>
<p> For Market	99   45,490   45,775</p>
<p>The 17 major states are Arkansas, Georgia, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, Nebraska, North Carolina, Oklahoma, Ohio, Pennsylvania, South Dakota and Wisconsin.  </p>
<p>For Market by Weight Groups (1,000 head):</p>
